{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1552553-demonic-form-ideas","id":1552553,"title":"Demonic Form Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-20T14:57:32-07:00","id":1552553,"title":"Demonic Form Ideas","content":"Hey guys I just wanted to create a thread where people could share their ideas for demonic forms. Here is one I was working on.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>Heart of the Machine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Type:</b> Process<br /> <br /> <b>Angelic Origin:</b><br /> <i>The God-Machine cannot be everywhere at once, and some missions are so critical that the agent's destruction would be a catastrophic failure. For these tasks, it designed angels with redundant systems\u2014fail-safes built into their very being. These angels carried a secondary &quot;heart,&quot; a quantum-entangled core matrix that could be detached and stored in a secure location. If the angel's primary form was compromised or destroyed during its mission, the God-Machine could reactivate the core, rebuilding the angel's pattern from the backup, ensuring the mission could be completed without the need to dispatch a new agent.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Adaptation:</b><br /> <i>For the Unchained, this ability is the ultimate defiance of the God-Machine's sentence. It is a promise that not even destruction is the end. A demon with this Process can literally leave a piece of their soul behind as a final anchor to the world, a contingency against the hunters and horrors that seek their end. They use it as a guarantee, a way to take incredible risks knowing they have a chance to come back from the brink. To have one's Heart destroyed is a terrifying experience, a reminder of the true mortality they now face.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b><br /> <i>When this Process is active, the demon\u2019s torso may show subtle signs of its nature. A faint, geometric seam might run over their chest, or their heartbeat might have a slight, metallic echo. The Heart itself, when removed, is a tangible object of about Size 1. It is never just a simple biological organ. It might be a clockwork device of brass and ticking gears, a pulsing crystal that gives off a faint warmth, a knot of humming copper wires, or a small, black iron cube that feels impossibly heavy. Whatever its form, it faintly beats in time with the demon's own pulse, no matter the distance.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> This Process allows the demon to create a redundant, external anchor for their soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 <b>Aether</b><br /> <b>Action:</b> The demon must spend one uninterrupted hour in a ritual to carefully excise the Heart of the Machine from their demonic form. This can only be done while in Full Demonic Form. Once the ritual is complete, the Heart is a physical object (Size 1, Durability equal to the demon's <b>Primum</b>, Structure equal to <b>Primum</b> + <b>Stamina</b>). The demon can then hide this Heart in a secure location. The demon can only have one external Heart active at a time. The demon instinctively knows the Heart's status and will feel a psychic shock if it is ever destroyed.<br /> <br /> The Heart of the Machine has two primary functions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Reformation:</b> If the demon is killed (their <b>Health</b> track is filled with Aggravated damage) or their body is completely destroyed, their consciousness instantly transfers to the external Heart's location. The Heart becomes the seed for a new body, which takes 24 hours to fully reform. The demon awakens in their human <b>Cover</b> (or as a Burned demon if they have no other Covers) with their <b>Health</b> track filled with Bashing damage except for the rightmost box, and with zero <b>Aether</b>. Any ongoing physical <b>Tilts</b> or <b>Conditions</b> are removed, but mental ones may remain at the Storyteller's discretion. If the demon is killed by a source that specifically targets or destroys souls, this power may not function.</li> <li><b>True Death:</b> This Process is the demon's only protection against death. If the external Heart is located and destroyed <i>before</i> the demon's body is killed, this ability offers no protection. If the demon dies while their external Heart is already destroyed, they die a true and final death. A demon can perform the hour-long ritual again to create a new Heart, but only after a full week has passed since the last one was destroyed.</li> </ol><br /> At <b>Primum 10</b>, when the demon gains a second Process, they can choose to take this ability a second time. This allows them to create and maintain two separate Hearts of the Machine in two different locations, granting them an additional layer of redundancy. If the demon is killed, their player chooses which Heart they reform at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}